        Tap any question to reveal the details.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
          <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p class="answer">
              Cats often purr when they feel relaxed and content, but they can also
              purr to self-soothe when they are anxious, tired, or recovering. The
              sound is thought to be created by rapid muscle movements in the larynx.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How much sleep do cats need?</span>
          <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p class="answer">
              Most adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day, and kittens or
              senior cats may sleep even more. Their natural hunting instincts make
              them conserve energy between active bursts of play and exploration.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Why do cats knead soft blankets or laps?</span>
          <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p class="answer">
              Kneading usually starts in kittenhood during nursing and can remain a
              comforting behavior into adulthood. Cats may knead when they feel safe,
              are preparing a cozy resting spot, or are marking an area with scent
              glands in their paws.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>What should cats eat for a healthy diet?</span>
          <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p class="answer">
              Cats are obligate carnivores, so they need food rich in animal protein
              and nutrients such as taurine. A balanced commercial diet formulated
              for their life stage is typically the safest foundation, with fresh
              water always available.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How can I help an indoor cat stay active?</span>
          <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p class="answer">
              Offer climbing spaces, scratchers, puzzle feeders, and short play
              sessions with wand toys or balls. Rotating toys and creating vertical
              areas near windows can keep an indoor cat mentally stimulated and
              physically engaged.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const items = document.querySelectorAll(".example");

    items.forEach((item) => {
      const button = item.querySelector(".question");
      const details = item.querySelector(".details");

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isOpen = item.classList.toggle("is-open");
        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(isOpen));
        details.hidden = !isOpen;
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
